            <div xml:id="d504-a1">

                <pb facs="0714" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg626"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 336.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum.</hi></head>
                <p>The Government of Venezuela knows that the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">South
                        Portland</hi>, which by the efforts of the Venezuelan minister at Washington
                    was detained in New York, has finally departed thence for Puerto Cabello,
                    carrying munitions of war, and asks your excellency to order the commanders of
                    your war ships anchored at La Guayra to repair to Puerto Cabello to prevent the
                    entrance of the revolutionary steamer, and defend the neutrality which the
                    United States should observe.</p>
                <p>The Venezuelan Government would be pained should your excellency not do it
                    justice in the premises.</p>
                <p>Received September 23, at 8:30 p.m.</p>
            </div>
